-- title:
--   Existence of the completed maximal unramified extension of ℤ_q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number. The assertion is the existence of a type $O^{nr}$ carrying a commutative ring structure which is an integral domain, a discrete valuation ring, and of characteristic zero, together with a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra structure on $O^{nr}$ and a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$ of $O^{nr}$, such that, writing $\mathfrak{p}$ for the ideal of $O^{nr}$ generated by the image of $q \in \mathbb{Z}_q$ under the structure map, the following five conditions hold: $O^{nr}$ is complete and separated for the $\mathfrak{p}$-adic filtration; $\mathfrak{p}$ is a maximal ideal; for every $x \in O^{nr}$ there is a monic polynomial $p$ with coefficients in $\mathbb{Z}_q$ whose value at $x$ (under the algebra map) lies in $\mathfrak{p}$; for every monic polynomial $p$ over $O^{nr}$ of positive degree there is an $x \in O^{nr}$ with $p(x) \in \mathfrak{p}$; and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^q \in \mathfrak{p}$ for every $x \in O^{nr}$. The last three conditions express, in terms of $O^{nr}$ alone, that the residue field $O^{nr}/\mathfrak{p}$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{F}_q$ and algebraically closed, and that $\mathrm{Fr}$ lifts the $q$-th power map on it.
--
--   This packages the completion of the maximal unramified extension of $\mathbb{Z}_q$ — equivalently the Witt vectors of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{F}_q$ — as a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with algebraically closed residue field and a Frobenius lift. It serves as the base ring for the Čerednik–Drinfeld material on fake elliptic curves and their moduli, and is cited in the construction of points over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ and in the study of stalks of the fine moduli problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PadicInt_exists_isAdicComplete_isMaximal_span_natCast_and_frobenius_sub_pow_mem.lean

